{"title":"2009 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc0d690868e31082e37790552b4480943852bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> is a straight line. What is the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7dd939779661bb1405ea97245ddd5d94390eb346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle RPS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63ae63b326d50f2e05126b4acd43b73e6a49b48f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 27^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 47^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 48^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 65^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 67^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"472\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e5014b756771402741d278144a552dd2a17321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle PRQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93cc7350d669858c051b6e5c8b9b0026fcb2e44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle PRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/9740ed03ad2a2353d2487a4bdda7cf3e8cd1345c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle RPS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can first use the fact that the sum of the interior angles of a triangle is always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />. Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, this means that we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6c3a1c5610028a35945f573e4d3e088ad3a2810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 67^{\\circ} + 48^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91ff501fd9eb50c5a76542cc4f449aa425ff1cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 115^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c7e4468e116ac13f56431b5c0425cceaeb67c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 180^{\\circ} - 115^{\\circ} = 65^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"179\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc0d690868e31082e37790552b4480943852bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> is a straight line, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8ceb33495e4e5268e0f6dbe696b6d5ba195c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must sum to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f07ae40c0ec4134ddd5d3368bcad13b8fa5c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + 65^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328a7bee1b437d4d31c90b5a41855ba0d0ed71a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 115^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can also now use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba18b40038d33882b310dc374cdcada01617e13d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle RPS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b51d8fd592c629c19b0a8af0d6842a7be55c033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z + 38^{\\circ} + 115^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876c1792e4eff1be3eda1f116b1d0b8779ada31a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z + 153^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b7772fc115949410d2c25f468f3fbd50da6674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 27^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"108\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93cc7350d669858c051b6e5c8b9b0026fcb2e44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle PRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/9740ed03ad2a2353d2487a4bdda7cf3e8cd1345c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle RPS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f09a667922e86574879c38c504bbcbfe85998732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle PRQ = 180 - [m\\angle QPR + m\\angle PQR]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"322\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/0/9903745252ad45c5309231a26555b337ee2353c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 180 - m\\angle PRQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc0c5574ceeffb2de94b2f6d5fd0fbe3224698eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 180 - (180 - [m\\angle QPR + m\\angle PQR])$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"325\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/6344f82dd5f3aeab8e980d9a56de5ba38d44553e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = m\\angle QPR + m\\angle PQR = 67^{\\circ} + 48^{\\circ} = 115^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"359\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can then use the same process as solution 1 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f597f0f883a22475e923853ab73b57da76073cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 27^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"108\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/9740ed03ad2a2353d2487a4bdda7cf3e8cd1345c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle RPS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcd5836b04224b1ac892cd555dd0e4bb9925cb3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle SPQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Using triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f575aad1d3f0e4d9224e9a8233e21c321c1bc72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" />, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e97168e5f83c6f52ad1febfdca3f6a486d208a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + 48^{\\circ} + 38^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed21e19b10e703739d4ce8cada85cb7826dcf92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + 86^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e0ebb173d6bd399ae66a92696340ddd9d168a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 94^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/2/e825e6ba91d5a4eaa4128046b29f26f2596c91a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle QPR + x = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />, giving:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/528043366a31426b4ae428c2402939ed6cac0658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 67^{\\circ} = 94^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b16214f52e5b99624ef2107833dfb3178630ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 27^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"109\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221806\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 238/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1793/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8633/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   10.878      1 -total\n 51.85%    5.641      6 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33758:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221806 and revision id 259898. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}